{{also|Karst|kärṣt-|kärst-}}
==English==
{{was wotd|2010|January|18}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Karst}}. The German term and the {{der|en|sl|-}} placename {{m|sl|Kras}} (the {{w|Karst Plateau (Italy-Slovenia)|Karst Plateau}}) are from {{der|en|sla-pro|*korsъ}}, from {{der|en|roa-itd}} ''carsus'' (cf. {{cog|it|carso}}), possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro||*ker-|t=hard; rock}}.<ref>Gams, I., Kras v Sloveniji — v prostoru in casu (Karst in Slovenia in space and time), 2003</ref> More at [[w:Karst#Etymology|Karst]].

The {{glossary|metathesis}} in the Slovene term precludes German borrowing from Slovene.

